WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.668
-You are known as a comedy fan.

00:00:02.668 --> 00:00:05.739
I would also say you're known
as a very funny comedian,

00:00:05.739 --> 00:00:07.273
as well, in your own right.

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:09.441
I would say --Who is --

00:00:09.441 --> 00:00:12.311
Who do you think the comedian
equivalent of you is?

00:00:12.311 --> 00:00:15.014
Who's at good at basketball
as a comedian as you --

00:00:15.014 --> 00:00:17.917
Is it Sandler? Is that the best
we have to offer?

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:19.518
-I mean, I would take that
in a heartbeat.

00:00:19.518 --> 00:00:20.920
He's also a good
basketball player.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.689
-That's what I mean.
So he has to be a comedian

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:24.290
who's as good at basketball

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:25.958
as you, a basketball player,
are at comedy.

00:00:25.958 --> 00:00:28.194
-Wow. Okay, I'll take that.
I like that. Yeah.

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:29.595
I'll take it. Thank you.

00:00:29.595 --> 00:00:32.698
-But I was seeing on Twitter
there was --

00:00:32.698 --> 00:00:35.134
Somebody showed up
at a Nets' press conference

00:00:35.134 --> 00:00:37.203
and asked Kevin Durant
some questions,

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:39.838
and it turned out
it was David Letterman.

00:00:39.838 --> 00:00:41.641
-Yeah, I was --

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:43.576
I was walking the hall --
Media Day is just crazy.

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:45.178
Everybody's going everywhere.

00:00:45.178 --> 00:00:47.847
I was walking the hallway to go
to one of my next stations,

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:49.315
and this guy turns the corner.

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:51.250
I kind of look up. I don't even
see his face or his profile.

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:54.621
He's just kind of walking
ahead of me.

00:00:54.621 --> 00:00:56.155
I'm like, "Boy, that looks
like David Letterman."

00:00:56.155 --> 00:00:57.690
But he has, like,
a T-shirt and jeans on,

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:00.927
and he's walking by himself in
the hallways of Barclays Center.

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:02.962
I'm like, "There's no way
that's David Letterman."

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:05.198
So I go about my business. I get
to the press-conference thing.

00:01:05.198 --> 00:01:07.266
One of the reporters is like,
"Did you see David Letterman?"

00:01:07.266 --> 00:01:09.936
I was like, "Why?

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:11.670
Why is David Letterman here?"

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:12.972
And then it turns out

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:14.740
he, you know, interviewed K.D.
a little bit.

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:16.842
-And were you --
were you bummed,

00:01:16.842 --> 00:01:19.512
one, that no one got you?

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:22.014
I would feel like somebody
should have been smart enough

00:01:22.014 --> 00:01:24.317
to go get Blake Griffin
if David Letterman was around.

00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:26.519
-Yeah, honestly, it's been
a point of contention

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:29.122
with the team.

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:30.690
Yeah, I would have loved
to have met him,

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:33.025
but I'm glad K.D.
got that moment.

00:01:33.025 --> 00:01:34.660
That was pretty cool.

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:36.563
-You had another moment

00:01:36.563 --> 00:01:38.297
with the dearly departed
Norm Macdonald,

00:01:38.297 --> 00:01:40.199
who you actually got to know
over the years.

00:01:40.199 --> 00:01:41.400
-I did. I did.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.869
He -- He surprised me
at a press conference.

00:01:43.869 --> 00:01:46.506
I did -- He had a show on
Comedy Central my rookie year,

00:01:46.506 --> 00:01:48.541
so I did a part of his show,

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:50.610
and then I went to go see him
do stand-up several times.

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:54.447
And he came to my charity event
one year, and --

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:56.382
Funniest guy ever.
-Funniest guy ever.

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:58.284
And then this --
I had not seen this,

00:01:58.284 --> 00:02:00.353
but somebody posted it online,
I think after --

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:02.822
And because David Letterman went
to this press conference.

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:03.923
But this is right after --

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:05.225
This was you giving
a press conference

00:02:05.225 --> 00:02:06.993
having won Rookie of the Year.
-Yes.

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:11.097
-And you did not know
that Norm was in the press pit.

00:02:11.097 --> 00:02:12.865
-I didn't.
I didn't know he was --

00:02:12.865 --> 00:02:15.100
Maybe I saw him,
but I didn't think

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:17.636
he was gonna ask a question.
There was just people there.

00:02:17.636 --> 00:02:19.138
He was basically
in the audience.

00:02:19.138 --> 00:02:21.073
He wasn't even in the press row.

00:02:21.073 --> 00:02:24.244
-It really is a perfect
Norm Macdonald joke...

00:02:24.244 --> 00:02:25.477
-Yeah.

00:02:25.477 --> 00:02:27.647
-...to ask the reigning
Rookie of the Year...

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:29.215
Let's take a look.

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:32.785
-It's a question from --
from Blake's good friend Norm.

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:35.788
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:38.457
Blake, it's fun watching you
this year. Wasn't it cool?

00:02:38.457 --> 00:02:39.491
-Yeah.
-Thank you.

00:02:39.491 --> 00:02:41.661
-And I was wondering.

00:02:41.661 --> 00:02:43.796
There's kind of a curse
with Rookie of the Year.

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:46.266
Nobody's ever repeated it.

00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:48.901
-Hmm. I didn't think about that.

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:51.937
Well, I'll try as hard
as I can next year, but...

00:02:51.937 --> 00:02:54.908
-All right, man.
-I don't know. I don't know.

00:02:54.908 --> 00:02:57.109
-So good.
-It's perfect.

00:02:57.109 --> 00:02:58.644
It's a perfect joke

00:02:58.644 --> 00:03:01.180
that has been there
for the taking forever.

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:04.317
Every time -- Ever since a sport
had Rookie of the Year.

00:03:04.317 --> 00:03:06.553
But what a nice moment.
-He was great, man.

00:03:06.553 --> 00:03:08.421
Like, when I met him,
I was like --

00:03:08.421 --> 00:03:10.489
I was so excited to meet him,
and then, you know,

00:03:10.489 --> 00:03:12.291
he does the thing
where he starts talking,

00:03:12.291 --> 00:03:14.460
and you're like,
"Where are we going with this?"

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:15.895
-Yeah.
-And then he just gets --

00:03:15.895 --> 00:03:18.497
He always finds it somehow.
He always finds it.

00:03:18.497 --> 00:03:21.334
And, like, seeing that in person
was like --

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:23.302
It was incredible for me.
-Yeah. It was really nice.

00:03:23.302 --> 00:03:24.737
It is fun to watch
the clip, too,

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:28.307
and watch the people around also
realize that's Norm Macdonald.

00:03:28.307 --> 00:03:29.508
-And then some people, like --

00:03:29.508 --> 00:03:31.211
He didn't get
that big of a laugh.

00:03:31.211 --> 00:03:32.946
-Right.
-That's a really good joke.

00:03:32.946 --> 00:03:36.149
I think people
were so thrown off --

00:03:36.149 --> 00:03:39.051
That's the perfect
Norm Macdonald...

00:03:39.051 --> 00:03:41.687
-Perfect. Absolutely. Perfect
execution, perfect joke.

00:03:41.687 --> 00:03:43.923
Last time we talked,
we talked about your podcast,

00:03:43.923 --> 00:03:45.225
"The Pursuit of Healthiness."

00:03:45.225 --> 00:03:46.992
-Yes.
-You just did a second season.

00:03:46.992 --> 00:03:48.961
Are you still enjoying that?
-I am. I am.

00:03:48.961 --> 00:03:51.763
It's really fun to, like, have
these conversations with people

00:03:51.763 --> 00:03:54.167
who are leading their fields
in health and wellness,

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:55.935
and I've got to talk
to some really,

00:03:55.935 --> 00:03:58.671
really interesting people,
and I love that stuff,

00:03:58.671 --> 00:04:00.373
so it's been a blast for me.

00:04:00.373 --> 00:04:01.707
-Do you find
when you're doing it

00:04:01.707 --> 00:04:03.576
that it goes faster
than you think it's going to go

00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:06.612
when you're having
the conversations?

00:04:06.612 --> 00:04:07.914
-After a while, yes.

00:04:07.914 --> 00:04:09.682
At first, I was so nervous,
I was like --

00:04:09.682 --> 00:04:11.184
I don't want to, like,
bore them.

00:04:11.184 --> 00:04:12.418
I don't want to do the thing

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:13.986
where I can't think
of the next question.

00:04:13.986 --> 00:04:15.754
So I was, like, constantly --
They'd be answering.

00:04:15.754 --> 00:04:19.125
I'd constantly be, like,
looking at my sheet,

00:04:19.125 --> 00:04:22.462
but also trying to make
eye contact at the same time.

00:04:22.462 --> 00:04:24.730
But, like, yeah,
as I did more and more,

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:27.499
like, the conversation
would just flow more naturally,

00:04:27.499 --> 00:04:30.102
and it was a little bit easier.

00:04:30.102 --> 00:04:31.471
It's not easy
interviewing people,

00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:34.106
but I have a blast doing it.

00:04:34.106 --> 00:04:35.408
-That's great.
Well, congrats on that.

00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:36.642
Best of luck
in the upcoming season.

00:04:36.642 --> 00:04:38.110
It's really nice
to have you here in person.

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:39.178
-Thank you, man.
I appreciate it.

00:04:39.178 --> 00:04:40.380
-You guys,
that's Blake Griffin.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:42.048
His podcast,
"The Pursuit of Healthiness,"

00:04:42.048 --> 00:04:43.616
is available exclusively
on Audible.

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:46.486
The NBA's 75th anniversary
season tips off on Tuesday,

00:04:46.486 --> 00:04:48.521
October 19th,
with the Brooklyn Nets

00:04:48.521 --> 00:04:51.090
facing the defending champs,
the Milwaukee Bucks.

